From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: iommu: sun55i: Drop the stale copy of struct iommu_dma_cookie

include/sunxi-iommu.h, which the sun55i IOMMU driver includes, carries
its own definition of struct iommu_dma_cookie (and of an enum
iommu_dma_cookie_type) copied from an old drivers/iommu/dma-iommu.c.
The structure is private to dma-iommu.c and has a different layout
there today (160 bytes vs 248 bytes, no "type" member). Nothing in the
sun55i driver uses either definition; they were dead code, but they
make two definitions of one struct name in the same kernel image.

struct iommu_domain points to struct iommu_dma_cookie, and struct
iommu_domain is reachable from struct device (device -> iommu ->
iommu_domain), struct fwnode_handle, struct irq_domain and many more.
BTF deduplication (pahole -J / libbpf btf__dedup) cannot merge two
type graphs that end in different struct iommu_dma_cookie bodies, so
vmlinux BTF kept three copies of struct device, and two or three
copies of 39 other types (fwnode_handle, irq_domain, platform_device,
...). Split (module) BTF then fails to resolve against the base:

  distilled base BTF type 'device' [10], size 784 has multiple
  candidates of the same size (ids [95063, 95062]) in base BTF
  failed to validate module [bifrost_kbase] BTF: -22

so out-of-tree modules built with distilled BTF are refused, and BPF
CO-RE relocations against those types are ambiguous.

Remove the stale enum and struct from the header. The driver builds
unchanged and vmlinux BTF has one struct device again.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 include/sunxi-iommu.h | 19 -------------------
 1 file changed, 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/sunxi-iommu.h b/include/sunxi-iommu.h
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/include/sunxi-iommu.h
+++ b/include/sunxi-iommu.h
@@ -28,23 +28,4 @@
 extern void sun55i_enable_device_iommu(struct sunxi_iommu_dev *iommu, unsigned int master_id, bool flag);
 extern void sun55i_reset_device_iommu(unsigned int master_id);
 
-enum iommu_dma_cookie_type {
-	IOMMU_DMA_IOVA_COOKIE,
-	IOMMU_DMA_MSI_COOKIE,
-};
-
-struct iommu_dma_cookie {
-	enum iommu_dma_cookie_type	type;
-	union {
-		/* Full allocator for IOMMU_DMA_IOVA_COOKIE */
-		struct iova_domain	iovad;
-		/* Trivial linear page allocator for IOMMU_DMA_MSI_COOKIE */
-		dma_addr_t		msi_iova;
-	};
-	struct list_head		msi_page_list;
-
-	/* Domain for flush queue callback; NULL if flush queue not in use */
-	struct iommu_domain		*fq_domain;
-};
-
 #endif  /* __LINUX_SUNXI_IOMMU_H */
